  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=\u27e83\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{5}\u27e9$ and $\\text{v}=\u27e8a,\\,10\u27e9$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 10-a\\cdot (-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =30\\sqrt{2}+a\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30\\sqrt{2}+a\\sqrt{5} & =0 \\\\ a\\sqrt{5} & =-30\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{10}}{5} \\\\ a & =-6\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
